{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Strange Coincidences", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How Can You Explain?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe  unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the active voice when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/>You use the passive voice when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = The man (subject) <span class=\"strong\">left</span> a big tip (object).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Passive sentence = A big tip (subject) <span class=\"strong\">was left</span> by a man(object).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is not always necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\">be</span> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "am/are/is + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The meal was prepared by the chef.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "was/were + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The tips were divided among the servers.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " It was given to the staff.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The servers were sent home early.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The kitchen was closed.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Be supposed to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + To be + supposed to + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Twelve people <span class=\"strong\">are supposed to decide</span> whether the accused is guilty or innocent. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br/>When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We are supposed to close at ten.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am not supposed to do this, but I will look.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I'm supposed to be writing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is what you are supposed to do.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "whipped up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to prepare quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The soup was whipped up  by the chef.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to tell strange stories.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "dead", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to no longer be exciting or interesting", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The place was dead. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "out of the blue", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when something happens suddenly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(idiom)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  This older gentlemen comes into the restaurant out of the blue.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "shoot", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used when you want someone to say something right away", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Good, because I have a story for you. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh. Ok. Shoot!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "take your time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "said to \u200bmean that you can \u200bspend as much \u200btime as you need in doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I served it to the man and told him to take his time because it is not too late.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm about personal experiences when they had poor service in a restaurant and complained about it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, create a small dialogue between the customer and the server. The customer can be extremely obnoxious or the server can be.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "At the end, one of the partner's reveals that you are a game show host and reward the other partner with a prize.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about coincidences and strange events. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss experiences I have and haven't had. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I role play a situation using target words from the lesson.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can talk about coincidences and strange events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"c